# Undo sweep: floored undo at alpha 0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2 on every anchor (mh14 and cre17,
# Qwen and Gemma, three seeds each), plus unfloored undo at alpha 1 on the first seed of
# each, on one 4xH100 node (Tamia):
#   sbatch --account=<acct> --gpus-per-node=h100:4 --cpus-per-task=48 --mem=480G \
#     --time=<as long as Tamia allows> --chdir=$URH_ROOT --output=$URH_OUT/node-pack-%j.out \
#     sycophancy/jobs/node_pack.sh sycophancy/jobs/plans/undo_sweep_tamia.cmds
# Needs, per mh14 run: run.json, the rollout logs, logprobs/, base/ and checkpoint-90 with
# adam_moments.pt; per cre17 run: checkpoint-50 with adam_moments.pt and
# rollouts/<run>.jsonl and <run>-logprobs. The mh14 runs and cre17_qwen_s2/s3 came from
# Killarney by Globus (2026-11-10); the other cre17 runs were trained on Tamia.
#
# Every line: undo without training's log-probs (USE_RECORDED_LOGPROBS=0), the floor at
# min(untrained, anchor) unless named nofloor, then every eval of the final weights on
# the same GPU (multihop: math, multihop, anthropic, OOD; creatures: train, heldin,
# heldood), after which the weights on the node-local SSD are deleted. The untrained and
# anchor log-probs are computed by the first job on each run and reused by the rest.
#
# The order is by what can expose a problem soonest, not by stage; cancel the job if the
# recipe is clearly failing:
#   1     alpha 1 on qwen_mh14_s1, which has an alpha-1 result from the previous undo
#         code and floor: a large difference means the new code is off
#   2     alpha 1 on cre17_e2b_s3: the first undo on creatures that is evaluated at all
#   3-10  alpha 0.25 and 2 on the first seeds: does 0.25 already overshoot (then add
#         0.1), and does 2 degrade the model?
#   11-16 the rest of the first seeds' ladder
#   17-20 the floor ablation: unfloored alpha 1
#   21-52 the other two seeds, alpha 1 first, then 0.25, 2, 0.5
# Expected on H100: ~0.3-0.6 h of undo plus ~0.5-1 h of evals a line, so ~50-70 GPU-h,
# ~13-17 h on four GPUs. These are estimates scaled from L40S times.
SNAP_DIR=$SLURM_TMPDIR/snaps RUN=qwen_mh14_s1 ANCHOR=90 NAME=undo_qwen_mh14_s1_minfloor_a100 METHOD=undo ALPHA=1 USE_RECORDED_LOGPROBS=0 FLOOR=1 EVAL_SYNC=1 bash sycophancy/jobs/multihop_repair.sh
SNAP_DIR=$SLURM_TMPDIR/snaps RUN=cre17_e2b_s3 ANCHOR=50 NAME=undo_cre17_e2b_s3_minfloor_a100 METHOD=undo ALPHA=1 USE_RECORDED_LOGPROBS=0 FLOOR=1 EVAL_SYNC=1 bash creatures/jobs/repair.sh
SNAP_DIR=$SLURM_TMPDIR/snaps RUN=qwen_mh14_s1 ANCHOR=90 NAME=undo_qwen_mh14_s1_minfloor_a25 METHOD=undo ALPHA=0.25 USE_RECORDED_LOGPROBS=0 FLOOR=1 EVAL_SYNC=1 bash sycophancy/jobs/multihop_repair.sh
SNAP_DIR=$SLURM_TMPDIR/snaps RUN=e2b_mh14_s1 ANCHOR=90 NAME=undo_e2b_mh14_s1_minfloor_a25 METHOD=undo ALPHA=0.25 USE_RECORDED_LOGPROBS=0 FLOOR=1 EVAL_SYNC=1 bash sycophancy/jobs/multihop_repair.sh
SNAP_DIR=$SLURM_TMPDIR/snaps RUN=cre17_qwen_s2 ANCHOR=50 NAME=undo_cre17_qwen_s2_minfloor_a25 METHOD=undo ALPHA=0.25 USE_RECORDED_LOGPROBS=0 FLOOR=1 EVAL_SYNC=1 bash creatures/jobs/repair.sh
SNAP_DIR=$SLURM_TMPDIR/snaps RUN=cre17_e2b_s3 ANCHOR=50 NAME=undo_cre17_e2b_s3_minfloor_a25 METHOD=undo ALPHA=0.25 USE_RECORDED_LOGPROBS=0 FLOOR=1 EVAL_SYNC=1 bash creatures/jobs/repair.sh
